      "text": "The record fixes no scheduled pickup time for this trip: trip_record.scheduled_at is null, and the platform's own derivation returns driver_deadline.deadline as null with the reason 'on-demand trip: no scheduled time' (the POL-NS-24 threshold of driver_late_after_scheduled_sec = 300 s has nothing to attach to). There is likewise no optimal or expected duration for the approach (optimal_duration_min is null), so the driver's ~5.5-minute run to the pickup cannot be tested against any benchmark either. POL-GEN-26 says that where a fact a rule of this version needs cannot be established the case is escalated, and under POL-GEN-03 an escalated case issues no monetary outcome and the amount is held rather than transferred. That matters here because the 5.00 SGD has already left the rider's card (fare_breakdown.payment_status 'CHARGED', refund_issued_sgd 0.0, charged_at 08:10:09), so a DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling would leave the rider carrying a charge whose premise the record never tests. The rider asks, in the alternative to a full refund, that the fee be held for a human reviewer rather than released to the driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05051", "EV-FARE-05051"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-24", "POL-GEN-26", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.driver_deadline.deadline",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The GPS trace holds no rider track at all (gps_trace.rider_track is empty), so no artifact on this record measures where the rider was during the 300-second free wait that POL-NS-21 requires to be served before a no-show fee attaches. The only thing on the record that says the rider was absent is the cancellation reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, which is the driver's own conclusion recorded at cancellation rather than a measurement of the rider's position or the rider's arrival at the car. POL-GEN-26 states that no outcome is inferred from the absence of evidence except where a rule says so, and the rule that must be satisfied here is POL-NS-21's free wait plus a rider no-show; that element is supported by the driver's characterisation alone. The gap should be resolved by a reviewer holding the fee, not by collecting it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-05051", "EV-TRIP-05051"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21", "POL-GEN-26"],
      "relies_on": "gps_trace.rider_track",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The third-party traffic advisory minted for this trip is absent: EV-ADVIS-05051-01 carries status MISSING, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT and weight_multiplier 0.0, and under POL-GEN-02(3) a MISSING artifact has weight 0.0 and carries no fact. The consequence is that the record contains no external account of road conditions on the morning in question, and that absence may not be read against the rider (POL-GEN-26). Taken with the absent scheduled pickup time and the absent expected-duration baseline, the record cannot test the driver's arrival obligation under POL-NS-24, so the case should be escalated and the 5.00 SGD held rather than released as driver compensation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05051-01"],
