  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 5.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 5.0,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the 5.00 SGD no-show fee stands, and it is confirmed as the driver's compensation.\n\nWhy the fee stands. The driver arrived at the pickup (Block 128, Lorong 1 Toa Payoh) at 08:04:20 (EV-TRIP-05051), and that arrival is independently corroborated by the driver-device GPS trace (EV-GPS-05051): the nearest fix to the pickup sits 3.74 m away with a reported accuracy of 4 m, inside POL-NS-21's 50 m arrival radius for a STANDARD pickup and inside the 25 m accuracy filter. The 300 s free wait therefore ran from 08:04:20 to 08:09:20, and the driver cancelled at 08:10:05 — 345 s after arrival, past the free wait (POL-NS-21). The driver's contact obligation under POL-NS-23 is met on both limbs: two in-app messages (08:04:40 'I'm at the drop-off point in front of Blk 128, grey Prius' and 08:08:30 'still coming down? I'm waiting') and one in-app call placed at 08:07:10 that rang 25 s unanswered — all before the 08:10:05 cancellation (EV-CHAT-05051, EV-TRIP-05051). The fare ledger (EV-FARE-05051) shows a single cancellation-fee line of 5.00 SGD and a total charged of 5.00 SGD, exactly POL-NS-22's fixed fee. The rider was notified at 08:04:24 and read both messages (08:05:14 and 08:08:50); the rider's only message of the trip came at 08:11:40, after the cancellation.\n\nOutcome. Under POL-NS-22, where the fee stands the ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION with amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd each equal to the fee charged, 5.00 SGD. That 5.00 SGD is the money this ruling moves to the driver; it is not a second payment and not a refund to the rider.\n\nThe rider's grounds for holding the fee do not displace it. (a) The record carries no scheduled pickup time (trip_record.scheduled_at is null). POL-NS-24's free-cancellation remedy is the rider's right to cancel at no charge when the driver fails to arrive by the scheduled time plus 5 minutes; this was an on-demand trip and the rider did not cancel — the driver did — so no scheduled time is a fact this dispute needs. Every fact the no-show rules require (the arrival, the 300 s wait, the message and the call, and the fee) is established, so POL-GEN-26 does not apply. (b) The GPS trace carries no rider track (gps_trace.rider_track is empty). POL-NS-21 requires the trip record and the GPS trace, not a measurement of the rider's own position; the rider's absence is shown by the served free wait together with the rider's own account that they came down late and their 08:11:40 message 'sorry coming now'. (c) The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-05051-01 is MISSING. Under POL-GEN-02(3) a MISSING artifact has weight 0.0 and carries no fact, and no rule that decides this case needs a traffic advisory; POL-GEN-26 does not infer an outcome from its absence.\n\nConfidence and who decides. Every artifact carrying a deciding fact — EV-TRIP-05051, EV-GPS-05051, EV-CHAT-05051 and EV-FARE-05051 — carries weight 1.0, so confidence is capped at 1.0; the bar here is 0.0. The amount contested is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD first band, so no confidence threshold applies and POL-NS-26 makes this AI ruling final. There is no safety flag (POL-GEN-21) and neither party carries a fraud flag. No referral fires: the amount charged is exactly the 5.00 SGD POL-NS-22 fixes; the POL-NS-24 goodwill credit does not arise because the driver arrived and attempted contact; and POL-NS-25's repeat no-show counter (rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d) is not present on the rider profile, so it is not applied."
  },
