{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 5.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 5.0,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver. This is the rider's dispute of the SGD 5.00 no-show cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-05051. The fee is valid and the SGD 5.00 goes to the driver as compensation.\n\nWhat the record shows. The ride was an on-demand booking, accepted 07:58:31. The driver arrived at the pickup at 08:04:20 and cancelled at 08:10:05 with reason RIDER_NO_SHOW; the fare ledger shows one SGD 5.00 cancellation-fee line, charged 08:10:09 (EV-TRIP-05051, EV-FARE-05051). Each element of a lawful no-show is carried by a complete, weight-1.0 artifact:\n- Free wait (POL-NS-21): the 300-second wait runs from the driver's arrival at 08:04:20 (the free_wait_start settled on arrived_at). The driver cancelled 345 seconds later, at 08:10:05 - 45 seconds beyond the wait. The arrival itself is corroborated, not taken on the platform's word: the nearest GPS fix sits 3.74 m from the pickup with reported accuracy 4 m, inside the 50 m STANDARD-pickup radius and the 25 m accuracy filter (EV-GPS-05051).\n- Contact obligation (POL-NS-23): the driver sent two in-app messages (08:04:40 and 08:08:30) and placed one in-app call (08:07:10, unanswered, 25 s), all before the 08:10:05 cancellation (EV-CHAT-05051, EV-TRIP-05051). Both limbs are met, so the fee is not voidable on this ground.\n- Fee amount (POL-NS-22): the amount charged is exactly the policy fee of SGD 5.00.\n\nThe rider's three points, and why they do not change the outcome. (1) The rider argues the record fixes no scheduled pickup time (scheduled_at null), so the driver's arrival obligation under POL-NS-24 cannot be tested and the case must be escalated under POL-GEN-26. POL-NS-24 gives the rider a free-cancellation right only where the driver fails to arrive by the scheduled time plus five minutes; it is a rider remedy the rider did not exercise, and on this record the driver did arrive at the pickup at 08:04:20. The clause never fires, and the fee does not rest on it: every fact the no-show rules need - the arrival, the served wait, the message and the call before cancellation, and the fee - is established, so there is no needed fact that is missing and POL-GEN-26 does not escalate. (2) The rider argues the GPS trace holds no rider track (rider_track empty), so nothing measures the rider's position during the wait. No clause in this category requires a rider track; the rider's absence is established without one, by the driver's contemporaneous message and call and by the rider's own message at 08:11:40 ('sorry coming now, where are you'), sent after the cancellation, together with the rider's own account of coming down late. (3) The rider cites the absent traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-05051-01 (status MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT). Under POL-GEN-02(3) a missing artifact carries no fact, and no no-show rule turns on road conditions; its absence is not read against either party and does not bear on whether the driver arrived, waited or made contact. I also note the rider's stated reason (a slow lift) engages no clause of this version.\n\nThe driver's points are accepted: the free wait was served (POL-NS-21), the contact obligation was met (POL-NS-23), the arrival is GPS-corroborated (POL-NS-21), and the fee is exactly the policy amount (POL-NS-22).\n\nOutcome. Because the no-show fee stands, POL-NS-22 directs a DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling of SGD 5.00: amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd both SGD 5.00 (the money the ruling moves to the driver - not a second payment and not a refund to the rider). No referral arises: POL-NS-22 adds one only where the amount charged differs from SGD 5.00 (here it is exactly 5.00); POL-NS-24's SGD 5.00 goodwill credit requires the driver to have failed to attempt contact (he messaged and called); and POL-NS-25 requires rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d, which is not present on this profile. This ruling is final: the SGD 5.00 contested is below POL-GEN-22's SGD 10.00 first band, so POL-NS-26 makes the AI ruling final at any confidence, and neither party carries a fraud flag. Confidence 0.95, within the cap of 1.0 set by the weight-1.0 artifacts that carry the deciding facts."
  },
